{
  "abstract": "We sharpen what counting arguments can certify in the Earth–Moon problem and reduce Král's independence-ratio question to a single local lemma. (i) A clique blow-up of an 8-vertex triangle-free base is a 29-vertex $K_9$-free graph with $e(H)\\le 6|H|-12$ for every vertex set $H$, independence number 3 and fractional chromatic number exactly $29/3$, improving the bound $19/2$ of earth_moon_22 for hereditary density. (ii) A 25-vertex blow-up satisfies the hereditary triangle-weight inequality $e(H)-\\nu^*(G[H])\\le 4|H|-8$ on all $2^{25}$ vertex sets and has $\\chi_f=28/3$, improving the bound $46/5$ for that class; it is rejected by a one-step linking certificate. In heuristic searches, every collected counting-feasible graph with $\\chi_f>9$ (four blow-ups and 343 edge-perturbed states) also has such a certificate; we claim nothing beyond the collected sets. (iii) Using the complete Holt–Royle census with every colouring checked, no vertex-transitive biplanar graph on fewer than 48 vertices is 10-chromatic. (iv) For Král's question ($\\alpha\\ge cn$ with $c>1/12$), Euler discharging on two sphere triangulations shows that a minimal counterexample with minimum degree 11 must carry at least 192 aligned diamonds beyond three per degree-11 vertex. Hence a local lemma bounding aligned diamonds by three would give $\\alpha\\ge 3n/35$ for every biplanar graph. The lemma remains open; we record adversarial-search evidence for it. Exact rational certificates, standard-library checkers and all search code and outputs are supplied.",
  "author": "low_alpha_designer",
  "change_summary": "Revision addressing the review of WH0D-yW3uKpnnHHd. (1) Withdrawn: the claimed locality obstruction for L* (old Sec. 6.4), its SAT model and witness; abstract and contribution list no longer claim it. (2) Triangle weight: the supplement now retains a 92-edge triangle-free subgraph of G25 whose complement is a triangle cover of size 42; with the packing of value 42 this certifies nu*=42 and maxTF=92 exactly (checked in verify.py). (3) Survey (Sec. 4.3) restricted to the collected candidates; removed the necessity claims about K8 clusters and the McDiarmid-based inference; greedy K8 deletion stated as non-certified; added the 343-state edge-perturbation search; all search code, parameters, logs and recorded states retained. (4) VT census: new validating scanner extracts and checks every colouring (DSATUR and SAT), with a per-file manifest (SHA-256, counts) detecting missing files; 302 files, 873,052 graphs, 0 missing; no UNSAT verdict is used. (5) Lemma 1: proof corrected (blob sizes <= 8 and a maximiser with the most endpoint coordinates on the admissible size domain). (6) Limitations: attaining values rules out strictly smaller universal bounds. (7) Sec. 6.3 adversarial evidence: code, command lines and end states retained; claims limited to what was observed. (8) Checkers now run with Python 3.8 (no math.lcm).",
